> ### ⚠ CORRECTION (2026-10-10) — the route IS real; one of this file's negative findings was wrong
> The 2026-10-09 pass above states "No OpenCode Zen ID" was confirmed and searched **OpenRouter**,
> which is a different provider. **OpenCode Zen does list `exo-free`.** Verified live on 2026-10-10
> against three Zen sources:
>
> | Zen source | Entry |
> |---|---|
> | Docs endpoint table | **Exo Free · `exo-free` · `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/chat/completions` · `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`** |
> | Pricing table | **Exo Free — Free / Free / Free** |
> | "The free models" list | **"Exo Free is available on OpenCode for a limited time. The team is using this time to collect feedback and improve the model."** |
>
> The folder's own `meta.json` was in fact accurate: *"OpenCode Zen's anonymous free route — 1M-token
> context with reasoning, tool calling, and image input at $0.00 while feedback is collected."*
>
> **The self-exclusion nonetheless still stands, on a different and stronger basis.** `exo-free` is a
> real *route* serving an **anonymous, undisclosed model**. Zen does not name the underlying weights,
> publishes no model card, no context figure, no modality table and no benchmarks for it — and Zen's
> own free-models list confirms it is a feedback-collection placeholder rather than a product.
> **Zero verified public benchmark numbers exist, which is the condition the template's rule tests.**
> What has changed is the *reason*: not "this route does not exist" but "this route exists, is free,
> and is deliberately undocumented."

> **Folder-health note (2026-10-10):** `model/exo-free/` now **is** listed in `model-queue.md` — it has
> an `average.md` and an active queue entry, so it was scaffolded into the roster after the 2026-10-09
> pass. The folder also now contains `Space_Bunny.md.excluded` (this file). **No deletion, relocation
